("h2","8.9 How to Identify and Change the Tense (Method)"),
("steps",[("Step 1 — Read the whole passage","Decide the general time (present, past, future). A narration of events is usually past; facts and habits are present."),("Step 2 — Find the signal words","yesterday, ago, last → past; since, for, just, already → perfect; now, these days → continuous; tomorrow, next → future."),("Step 3 — Pick the aspect","Habit → indefinite; in progress → continuous; completed with link to now/another time → perfect; duration → perfect continuous."),("Step 4 — Check the helping verb","do/does/did + V1; am/is/are/was/were + V-ing; has/have/had + V3; will/shall + V1.")]),
